//@version=6
indicator("UCTPROBE_VW_INPUT_TIME_MEMBER", overlay = false)

// PROVENANCE: written 2026-11-07 for the Pine parity programme, capture queue row Q-D3
// (docs/pine/capture-queue-2026-10-31-wsd-input-kinds.md). NEVER COMPILED ON TRADINGVIEW.
// Q-D1's shape, captured TWICE: once at the default, then after the time is changed in
// TradingView's settings dialog. Record the date and time the dialog SHOWS for the default and the
// value typed; T01 is the UNIX-ms instant the run received, D01 the first bar plotting 1. The
// question: does the dialog show and take the time in the chart's (exchange) zone or in UTC?
// CAPTURE: AMEX:SPY 1D. Capture 1 at defaults; capture 2 with t set in the dialog to a time of
// the capturer's choosing (e.g. 21 Feb 2020 00:00): record it as typed and the dialog's zone label, if any.

t = input.time(timestamp("20 Feb 2020"), "t")

plot(bar_index, "A00_bar_index_CONTROL")
plot(t, "T01_t_ms")
plot(time >= t ? 1 : 0, "D01_time_ge_t")
